Parentheses around a first command that calls html or urlquery stay in a
plain action without declarations. html/template checks only that pipeline
for predefined escapers, allows them only as its last command, and does not
look inside a parenthesized one, so flattening it would make html/template
reject the template (PR #208 review). Elsewhere (a branch header, a
declaration, an argument) html/template does not check, and the
parentheses go as they do around any other call. A parenthesized first
command that calls neither is flattened too.
-- input.gohtml --
<p>{{ (html .Name) | printf "%s" }}</p>
<a href="/q?{{ (urlquery .Name) | printf "q=%s" }}">x</a>
<p>{{ (printf "%s" .Name) | html }}</p>
<p>{{ (html .Name) }}</p>
<p>{{if (html .Name)}}y{{end}}</p>
<p>{{$x := (html .Name)}}{{$x}}</p>
<p>{{printf "%s" ((html .Name))}}</p>
-- format.gohtml --
<p>{{(html .Name) | printf "%s"}}</p>
<a href="/q?{{(urlquery .Name) | printf "q=%s"}}">x</a>
<p>{{printf "%s" .Name | html}}</p>
<p>{{(html .Name)}}</p>
<p>{{if html .Name}}y{{end}}</p>
<p>{{$x := html .Name}}{{$x}}</p>
<p>{{printf "%s" (html .Name)}}</p>
-- data/empty.json --
{}
-- data/truthy.json --
{"Name":"a<b&c"}
